 <div class="sec-head rv" style="margin-top:78px"><div class="eyebrow"><span class="bundle-mark"><img src="https://www.zohowebstatic.com/sites/zweb/images/productlogos/social.svg" alt=""><img src="https://www.zohowebstatic.com/sites/zweb/images/productlogos/crm.svg" alt=""><img src="https://www.zohowebstatic.com/sites/zweb/images/productlogos/books.svg" alt=""><img src="https://www.zohowebstatic.com/sites/zweb/images/productlogos/desk.svg" alt=""><b>Elite Tech Corp</b></span><em>Return on investment</em></div><h2 class="">A signed preschool territory is worth<br>a fee plus <span class="hl">years of royalty.</span></h2><p class="lede">A hundred parent enquiries you are not fulfilling are worth roughly nothing to the franchisor. One qualified investor who signs a franchise agreement is worth a franchise fee plus years of campus royalty. That asymmetry is the whole ROI argument, and the loop is built so no investor is lost to a missed handoff.</p></div>
 <div class="roigrid st" style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(4,1fr);gap:18px;margin-top:44px">
 <div class="roicard"><span class="ri"><i class="fa-solid fa-magnet"></i></span><h4>Grow: no preschool investor missed</h4><p>Investment intent tagged around the clock, from franchise opportunity comments to page visitors, and the opportunity page tested for qualified leads, not raw clicks.</p></div><div class="roicard"><span class="ri"><i class="fa-solid fa-location-dot"></i></span><h4>Close: one prospect per city</h4><p>Preschool territories reserved during active talks, and franchise agreements signed in sequence in days, not weeks of courier and scan.</p></div><div class="roicard"><span class="ri"><i class="fa-solid fa-arrows-rotate"></i></span><h4>Run: campus revenue on autopilot</h4><p>Royalty billed from declared campus revenue every month, with franchisee support in an SLA tracked queue that keeps every preschool location productive.</p></div><div class="roicard"><span class="ri"><i class="fa-solid fa-seedling"></i></span><h4>Loop: referrals compound</h4><p>Supported preschool franchisees refer the next investor and renew informed, feeding the top of the funnel for free.</p></div>
 </div>
 <div class="ba rv" style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;gap:20px;margin-top:24px">
 <div class="ba-col ba-before"><h4><i class="fa-solid fa-xmark"></i> Before</h4><ul><li>A future franchisee likes a preschool post and nothing happens next</li><li>A franchise enquiry sits in an inbox over the weekend while the investor cools</li><li>Two prospects promised the same city for their preschool campus</li><li>A signed franchisee waits weeks for the first royalty invoice</li></ul></div>
 <div class="ba-col ba-after"><h4><i class="fa-solid fa-check"></i> After</h4><ul><li>Investment intent tagged and scored from every franchise opportunity signal</li><li>The territory question answered live in chat, discovery call booked</li><li>The city reserved the moment franchise talks begin, double selling impossible</li><li>Signature creates the campus record and schedules royalty billing at once</li></ul></div>
 </div>
 </div></section>
<section class="sec sec--alt" id="faq">
 <div class="box">
 <div class="sec-head center rv" style="margin-bottom:40px"><div class="eyebrow"><span class="bundle-mark"><img src="https://www.zohowebstatic.com/sites/zweb/images/productlogos/social.svg" alt=""><img src="https://www.zohowebstatic.com/sites/zweb/images/productlogos/crm.svg" alt=""><img src="https://www.zohowebstatic.com/sites/zweb/images/productlogos/books.svg" alt=""><img src="https://www.zohowebstatic.com/sites/zweb/images/productlogos/desk.svg" alt=""><b>Elite Tech Corp</b></span><em>FAQ</em></div><h2 class="">Before you connect the loop,<br><span class="hl">the questions that come up</span></h2><p class="lede">The questions preschool franchise brands ask before they connect the loop.</p></div>
 <div class="faqcol">
 <div class="qa rv open"><button aria-expanded="true">How do you actually tell a franchise enquiry apart from an admission enquiry at the point of contact?<span class="pm"></span></button><div class="ans"><div><p>Mostly through where they land. A &quot;Become a Franchise Partner&quot; page and a &quot;Find a Campus&quot; page ask different questions from the first field onward. A chatbot can also ask directly within the first exchange if the intent is not obvious yet.</p></div></div></div><div class="qa rv"><button aria-expanded="false">Is it risky to route admission leads without any further follow up on your end?<span class="pm"></span></button><div class="ans"><div><p>The lead is not abandoned. It is handed to the party actually equipped to act on it, immediately, with a notification confirming it landed. What stops is your team doing work that belongs to the franchisee, not the lead itself getting attention.</p></div></div></div><div class="qa rv"><button aria-expanded="false">What does qualifying a franchise applicant actually involve?<span class="pm"></span></button><div class="ans"><div><p>Capital available, proposed city or territory, relevant background, sometimes a basic credit or reference check. The same seriousness you would want if you were the one deciding whether to license your name to someone.</p></div></div></div><div class="qa rv"><button aria-expanded="false">Can a franchisee see admission leads routed to their campus without seeing your franchise pipeline?<span class="pm"></span></button><div class="ans"><div><p>Yes. A franchisee's access is scoped entirely to their own campus. The prospects you are currently qualifying to open new locations stay visible only to your team.</p></div></div></div><div class="qa rv"><button aria-expanded="false">We only have a few franchise locations right now. Is any of this premature?<span class="pm"></span></button><div class="ans"><div><p>The earlier this split exists, the less untangling you will need to do later. Most of the mess we get called in to fix is a franchisor whose admission handling and franchise recruitment quietly merged into one confused pipeline over a few years of growth.</p></div></div></div><div class="qa rv"><button aria-expanded="false">Does a new franchisee's campus plug into this system automatically once they are onboarded?<span class="pm"></span></button><div class="ans"><div><p>Yes. Signing triggers their territory assignment, and from that point their campus starts receiving admission leads for its area the same way every other location does.</p></div></div></div>
 </div>
 </div>
</section>
