<section class="sec sec--alt" id="faq">
 <div class="box">
 <div class="sec-head center rv" style="margin-bottom:40px"><div class="eyebrow"><span class="bundle-mark"><img onerror="this.style.opacity='0'" referrerpolicy="no-referrer" src="https://www.zohowebstatic.com/sites/zweb/images/productlogos/social.svg" alt=""><img onerror="this.style.opacity='0'" referrerpolicy="no-referrer" src="https://www.zohowebstatic.com/sites/zweb/images/productlogos/crm.svg" alt=""><img onerror="this.style.opacity='0'" referrerpolicy="no-referrer" src="https://www.zohowebstatic.com/sites/zweb/images/productlogos/books.svg" alt=""><img onerror="this.style.opacity='0'" referrerpolicy="no-referrer" src="https://www.zohowebstatic.com/sites/zweb/images/productlogos/desk.svg" alt=""><b>Elite Tech Corp</b></span><em>FAQ</em></div><h2 class="">Zoho Social for preschool franchises,<br><span class="hl">answered</span></h2><p class="lede">Straight answers about Zoho Social for preschool franchise brands.</p></div>
 <div class="faqcol">
 <div class="qa rv open"><button aria-expanded="true">How is a franchise enquiry told apart from general engagement?<span class="pm"></span></button><div class="ans"><div><p>Franchise specific keywords and page context automatically tag investment related comments and messages.</p></div></div></div><div class="qa rv"><button aria-expanded="false">Can we run this alongside existing franchise opportunity handles?<span class="pm"></span></button><div class="ans"><div><p>Yes, dedicated channels are supported alongside your main brand presence.</p></div></div></div><div class="qa rv"><button aria-expanded="false">Do we need heavy posting volume for this to work?<span class="pm"></span></button><div class="ans"><div><p>No, a focused, well tagged calendar outperforms high volume, untargeted posting.</p></div></div></div><div class="qa rv"><button aria-expanded="false">Can we see which specific post generated a signed franchisee?<span class="pm"></span></button><div class="ans"><div><p>Yes, attribution is tracked from the original post through to the CRM lead and its outcome.</p></div></div></div><div class="qa rv"><button aria-expanded="false">What happens if a comment is ambiguous?<span class="pm"></span></button><div class="ans"><div><p>It’s logged for manual review rather than being force classified incorrectly.</p></div></div></div>
 </div>
