<section class="sec sec--alt" id="faq">
 <div class="box">
 <div class="sec-head center rv" style="margin-bottom:40px"><div class="eyebrow"><span class="bundle-mark"><img onerror="this.style.opacity='0'" referrerpolicy="no-referrer" src="https://www.zohowebstatic.com/sites/zweb/images/productlogos/social.svg" alt=""><img onerror="this.style.opacity='0'" referrerpolicy="no-referrer" src="https://www.zohowebstatic.com/sites/zweb/images/productlogos/crm.svg" alt=""><img onerror="this.style.opacity='0'" referrerpolicy="no-referrer" src="https://www.zohowebstatic.com/sites/zweb/images/productlogos/books.svg" alt=""><img onerror="this.style.opacity='0'" referrerpolicy="no-referrer" src="https://www.zohowebstatic.com/sites/zweb/images/productlogos/desk.svg" alt=""><b>Elite Tech Corp</b></span><em>FAQ</em></div><h2 class="">Zoho PageSense for preschool franchises,<br><span class="hl">answered</span></h2><p class="lede">Straight answers about Zoho PageSense for preschool franchise brands.</p></div>
 <div class="faqcol">
 <div class="qa rv open"><button aria-expanded="true">Is franchise page traffic enough to test reliably?<span class="pm"></span></button><div class="ans"><div><p>It’s lower than admissions traffic, so tests run longer and lean more on recordings and heatmaps.</p></div></div></div><div class="qa rv"><button aria-expanded="false">Does testing risk showing inconsistent pages to prospects?<span class="pm"></span></button><div class="ans"><div><p>No, traffic is split automatically and cleanly within a single test cycle.</p></div></div></div><div class="qa rv"><button aria-expanded="false">Will a test that lowers total leads ever be the right call?<span class="pm"></span></button><div class="ans"><div><p>Yes, if qualified leads and discovery calls booked rise, that’s the metric that matters.</p></div></div></div><div class="qa rv"><button aria-expanded="false">How long does a typical test take to reach significance?<span class="pm"></span></button><div class="ans"><div><p>Usually three to six weeks for franchise pages, given lower traffic volumes.</p></div></div></div><div class="qa rv"><button aria-expanded="false">Can we test more than one element at a time?<span class="pm"></span></button><div class="ans"><div><p>It’s possible, but running fewer, focused tests on low traffic pages produces more reliable results.</p></div></div></div>
 </div>
</section>
